# Framing policy for the embed. Consumed by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages. On other
# hosts translate these to the equivalent config (staticwebapp.config.json on
# Azure, `add_header` on nginx/Caddy, a Route annotation on Rahti/OpenShift).
#
# X-Frame-Options is deliberately NOT set: any value of it would block framing,
# and it has no allowlist. frame-ancestors is the modern replacement.
#
# `*` allows any host to frame this while the deploy target is being decided.
# Tighten it to the real hosts before production, e.g.
#   Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' https://opensuperqplus.eu
/embed/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
